WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.980
I want to talk today about the phrase Trump
derangement syndrome.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.959
I've tweeted about this a few times, and Chauncey
de Vega wrote a really good article about

00:00:10.959 --> 00:00:14.440
this on Salon, which I tweeted yesterday,
called.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.630
There was no Trump derangement syndrome.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.700
We were right about him all along.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.070
So let's talk about this.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:26.660
Trump derangement syndrome is a bad faith
phrase which is meant to shut down debate,

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.350
stop conversation and excuse Donald Trump's
atrocious behavior.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.530
Now, I know that there will certainly be some
of you who will respond to me and say, you

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.530
know, David, look.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.940
Check out this person on Twitter who is irrationally
obsessed with everything Trump does.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.850
And they think anything bad in the world is
Trump's doing.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.180
This person is suffering from Trump derangement
syndrome.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:51.510
Listen, you you can find instances of everything
on the Internet, but we're not dealing in

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.840
anecdotes here.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:58.060
The problem systemically with the phrase Trump
derangement syndrome is that its use is very

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.400
similar to what Regressive left became a couple
of years ago.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.900
I don't know if you remember this, but regressive
left much like Trump derangement syndrome

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:11.630
are phrases that are used to shut down debate
by disqualifying and dismissing criticism

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.890
without actually having to debate the merits
of the criticism.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.350
So let's first really dig in.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.530
I want everybody to get this.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.940
What do people mean by Trump derangement syndrome?

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:28.190
The idea of TADS, as it's sometimes called,
is to use it as a retort.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.350
When someone criticizes Donald Trump, someone
says, look.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.540
Trump did this.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.760
Well, Trump's not responsible for 160000 deaths,
but he's responsible for some because it's

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.010
been one of the worst responses to the virus
in the world.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.189
You have Trump derangement syndrome.

00:01:43.189 --> 00:01:49.729
And what they mean by that is you are so blinded
by your hatred of Donald Trump that we can

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:54.940
dismiss what you are saying without examining
it, because you're just blinded by your rage

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.630
against Donald Trump.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.400
So think back to the term regressive left.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.520
There was this very, very brief period where
the term regressive left was sort of interesting

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:10.200
and that it was used to describe instances
of ostensible or supposed leftists failing

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.680
to actually be on the left in their views.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:17.910
And typically what you had was instances of
people who claimed to be on the left being

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:18.980
authoritarian.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.050
And in a sense, it was a useful term for a
very short period of time.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:28.620
And very quickly, the term regressive left
was bastardized and perverted by the right.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.620
And it became a.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.040
Catchall insult that they used to basically
say, you're on the left and I don't like what

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.040
you have to say.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.790
I don't like what you're saying because it's
left wing and regressive, left, lost all value

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:44.200
as as any kind of a useful tool to explore.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.340
Failing to be on the left.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:52.209
Trump derangement syndrome is equally meaningless
with the important difference that, unlike

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:57.020
regressive, left, Trump derangement syndrome
never actually described a real thing.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.069
It was always bogus.

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:02.390
There was a brief period where Regressive
Left actually was an interesting term to describe

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:07.650
something I had been talking about for for
many years, which are instances of the authoritarian

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.600
left failing to really be on the left.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.480
But with each passing day, the most serious
concerns about Donald Trump that were expressed

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.830
by people on the left like me have been proven
to be true and they've been proven to be true,

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:21.830
horrifyingly.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.851
So remember that months ago Joe Biden was
widely ridiculed for suggesting, you know,

00:03:25.851 --> 00:03:31.180
Trump might try to create some kind of pretext,
that emergency of some kind to delay the election.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.670
Trump did that days ago by tweeting.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.959
Maybe we do need to delay the election.

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:41.370
Joe Biden was ridiculed and said he was you
know, people were saying he has Trump derangement

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.370
syndrome.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.370
He was right.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:48.459
Years ago, people raised the alarm about Donald
Trump's authoritarian tendencies.

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:50.970
Sort of he wants to be a he's a wannabe dictator.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:56.840
And over the last month, we have seen him
send armed paramilitaries to American cities

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.590
to throw people into unmarked vans.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.200
And has Chauncy de Vega points out, points
out in the article that we're linking to which

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.909
you should read, quote.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:10.120
This was a phrase used to demean, mock, reject,
dismiss and deflect warnings about Donald

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.810
Trump's beliefs and tendencies.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:18.559
And those who were trying to raise the alarm
were called, again, as Chauncy says, hysterical,

00:04:18.559 --> 00:04:23.639
alarmist or out of touch and bitter about
Hillary Clinton's loss.

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:28.229
If you encounter the phrase Trump derangement
syndrome on the Internet, on Twitter and on

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:30.270
in real life may be anywhere.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.139
Don't allow yourself to be bullied into silence
by it.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:36.719
They claim on the right that they're all about
conversation.

00:04:36.719 --> 00:04:42.139
And yet this entire idea of Trump derangement
syndrome is meant to stop conversation.

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:47.349
Make it clear that calling someone a victim
of Trump derangement syndrome is not really

00:04:47.349 --> 00:04:48.439
an argument.

00:04:48.439 --> 00:04:51.039
Say, I'm glad to talk about that.

00:04:51.039 --> 00:04:52.789
Which facts that I get wrong.

00:04:52.789 --> 00:04:54.669
I'm glad to change my views.

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:59.050
If you tell me what I got wrong, Trump derangement
syndrome is not an argument.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.050
It's a smokescreen.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.599
It tries to put us on the defensive.

00:05:02.599 --> 00:05:07.370
But the real derangement is the more than
60 million people, nearly 63 million people

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:10.039
who voted for Donald Trump in 2016.

00:05:10.039 --> 00:05:14.110
Tens of millions of whom plan to vote for
him again in just months.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.750
That's the real derangement.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:24.149
The horrifying nature of this presidency,
which will be affirmed by 50, 60, 65, 67 million

00:05:24.149 --> 00:05:28.430
people who plan to vote for it again in November.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:34.330
If there is any valid criticism of those like
me on the anti Trump side, it's that we didn't

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:38.809
do enough to raise the alarm prior to him
being elected as much as I tried.

00:05:38.809 --> 00:05:43.319
Now, of course, the people who are primarily
to blame are the people who fell for it and

00:05:43.319 --> 00:05:44.800
voted for Trump.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.080
But if you want to make a criticism of the
anti Trump left, that is to be taken more

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.680
seriously.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:54.729
Criticize us for something real, which is
that as much as many of us were trying to

00:05:54.729 --> 00:06:00.550
warn people, even we might have underestimated
the risks of the presidency.

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:02.149
That's the reality.

00:06:02.149 --> 00:06:03.389
Trump derangement syndrome.

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:08.249
Don't allow it to be used to silence actual
critiques of this president, which, if anything,

00:06:08.249 --> 00:06:11.789
have been not alarmist enough.

00:06:11.789 --> 00:06:13.080
Let me know your thoughts.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.839
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:06:14.839 --> 00:06:19.680
And remember, you can get the daily audio
podcast every day, 3:00 p.m. Eastern on your

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.822
favorite podcasting app, whichever one it
may be.

